", "title": "Distributional effects"}, {"id": "a8b31204-5127-44d5-b324-122b7b95d1f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Targeting"}, {"id": "306d333a-c8c0-4861-ad27-9fdcd7d30b47", "type": "concept", "title": "Unintended consequences"}], "description": "Microeconomics asks not only whether a policy is efficient but also how it distributes outcomes."}]}, {"id": "162c5a19-c2da-4a3c-943e-0508067f7136", "type": "topic", "title": "Information, Behavioral Economics, and Decision Biases", "description": "Explore how hidden information and bounded rationality change market outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "5d4cd7e8-f01f-4c93-b5c9-d316af01272c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Information problems", "children": [{"id": "6e1ccb82-58ce-4a55-9ae3-04f1ea00a512", "type": "concept", "title": "Adverse selection"}, {"id": "ef954f5f-3536-4799-8a64-37ab91449171", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral hazard"}, {"id": "a400e1eb-88c4-4289-8809-1eb8b5d7ce46", "type": "concept", "title": "Signaling"}, {"id": "798028e9-85d6-44f3-acd6-d0c38f57c7d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening"}], "description": "Hidden information can prevent markets from working well."}, {"id": "0d7d1ce7-cf12-431b-8b24-25a54fd1f189", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral economics", "children": [{"id": "e361a6cd-81b4-4b22-bdcc-f84576ab441e", "type": "concept", "title": "Bounded rationality"}, {"id": "0f359a3d-b0d5-4056-bf86-5863a5fb7187", "type": "concept", "title": "Loss aversion"}, {"id": "e432729d-2eae-49e8-a0f9-5426146f9f9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Present bias"}, {"id": "e7f13563-96d8-45a7-b695-35296a3c3454", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental accounting"}], "description": "Behavioral economics studies systematic ways people depart from the standard rational model."}, {"id": "eaeb17fb-3825-4c1e-b8d2-1673154a0353", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Choice architecture", "children": [{"id": "22d96610-12f3-4c19-81ad-cb91e85acc70", "type": "concept", "title": "Defaults"}, {"id": "a8d7f571-9eba-4d01-a5e6-25d46f0f6311